From: ste <ste@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: preserve requested size for shared BOs

Shared BOs are never returned to the reuse cache, but the allocation path
still rounds them to a cache bucket.  Besides wasting memory, this makes an
exported dma-buf larger than its externally described image layout.  Some
Android gralloc importers require those sizes to match exactly.

Bypass cache-bucket selection for FD_BO_SHARED allocations while retaining
page alignment.
---
 src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_bo.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_bo.c b/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_bo.c
index 6eda8101e46c..826b370c2033 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_bo.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_bo.c
@@ -137,9 +137,18 @@ bo_new(struct fd_device *dev, uint32_t size, uint32_t flags,
    if ((flags & FD_BO_CACHED_COHERENT) && !dev->has_cached_coherent)
       flags &= ~FD_BO_CACHED_COHERENT;
 
-   bo = fd_bo_cache_alloc(cache, &size, flags);
-   if (bo)
-      return bo;
+   /* Shared BOs are never returned to the reuse cache, so rounding them to a
+    * cache bucket only wastes memory.  It can also make the exported dma-buf
+    * larger than the externally described image layout, which some importers
+    * reject.  Preserve only the allocator's page-size requirement.
+    */
+   if (flags & FD_BO_SHARED) {
+      size = align(size, os_page_size);
+   } else {
+      bo = fd_bo_cache_alloc(cache, &size, flags);
+      if (bo)
+         return bo;
+   }
 
    bo = dev->funcs->bo_new(dev, size, flags);
    if (!bo)
